{"cluster_id": "C-4036", "topic": "The new CAS S3 functional-test CI lane calls `CH", "target": "operations/migration", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-075"], "canonical_claim": "The new CAS S3 functional-test CI lane calls `CH.start_rustfs()`, which only checks for a pre-existing `ci/tmp/rustfs` binary and returns `False` if missing; unlike `setup_minio.sh` for MinIO, no tracked script downloads/extracts the RustFS binary, so the lane fails deterministically on a clean CI runner. Fix direction: add a tracked `setup_rustfs.sh` mirroring `setup_minio.sh` that pulls/extracts the `rustfs/rustfs:1.0.0-beta.8` static binary into `ci/tmp/rustfs`, invoked before the CAS s3 job's `start()`.", "issue_ids": ["P1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-06-scenario-validation-night.md#notes"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4037", "topic": "unused ProfileEvents", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-243", "B002-076", "B013-043"], "canonical_claim": "Six ProfileEvents\u2014`ContentAddressedGenerationResurrectionsTotal`, `ContentAddressedDuplicateGenerationBytes`, `ContentAddressedTombstonesTotal`, `ContentAddressedGenerationsObserved`, `ContentAddressedHashesObserved`, and `ContentAddressedOrphanBytesEstimate`\u2014have zero increment sites and describe a removed design. Risk register #9 (Medium, confirmed): six `ContentAddressed*` `ProfileEvents` (`ProfileEvents.cpp:876-881`) have zero increment sites, relics of the pre-rebuild generation/tombstone GC design; always-zero counters imply \"no resurrections/orphans\" on dashboards, which is actively misleading. Suggested action: delete them after verifying no dashboard depends on them. The zero-increment `ProfileEvents` for removed shard mutation queues, pre-rebuild GC, manifest backpressure, and part-folder-view evictions, plus the unused `GcSnapPersist` event, are removed after confirming no increment sites or dashboard consumers.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L1445-L1482", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L550", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/04-ops-mounts.md#8-weak-places", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup-design.md#L135-L151"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4038", "topic": "dropped mount audit events", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-249", "B002-078"], "canonical_claim": "Mount events emitted inside `Store::open` are dropped because the CA event sink is installed only after open completes. Risk register #15 (Low, confirmed): mount events emitted inside `Store::open` (`CasStore.cpp:331-337`) are dropped because the event sink is installed only after `open` returns, so first-mount claim/conflict decisions never reach `system.content_addressed_log`. Suggested action: pre-install the sink before `open` if first-mount audit matters.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L556", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/04-ops-mounts.md#8-weak-places"]}
