{"cluster_id": "C-4045", "topic": "retry-later error observability", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B018-006", "B018-015"], "canonical_claim": "CAS retry-later failures were opaque because the message said `retry budget exhausted` even for a pre-attempt fence rejection, and the failures were logged at Information level without populating `system.replication_queue.last_exception`. The retry-later helper's message carries the precise cause, and changing the escaping error to non-exempt `NETWORK_ERROR` automatically populates `system.replication_queue.last_exception` and `last_exception_time` through existing merge handling.", "issue_ids": ["#37"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-16-cas-merge-upload-retry-fix-design.md#defects", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-16-cas-merge-upload-retry-fix-design.md#fix-opacity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4046", "topic": "Review finding \u211630 is real for started disks: `system", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B019-087"], "canonical_claim": "Review finding \u211630 is real for started disks: `system.content_addressed_mounts` skips listing exceptions and can make a failed listing appear as no mounts, although not-started disks are legitimately skipped.", "issue_ids": ["\u211630"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L453-L459", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L50-L50"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4047", "topic": "The initial S23 RSS failure was allocator retention and fresh-boot warmu", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-173", "B020-020"], "canonical_claim": "The initial S23 RSS failure was allocator retention and fresh-boot warmup rather than a GC or log-flushing leak: the 86-second empty-pool run had sawtooth RSS, while `MemoryTracking` grew only about 50\u201370 MiB and the remainder was allocator dirty-page residency.; S23's initial idle-RSS-growth failure correlated with elevated S3 error rates in the same window (read 8.6%, write 17.2% on one node); S3 retries allocate transient upload/download buffers that jemalloc keeps resident as dirty pages, inflating RSS without inflating tracked memory, which is one of two identified amplifiers of the outlier (the other being fresh-boot warmup variance).", "issue_ids": ["S23"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s23-idle-rss-rca.md#L33-L40", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s23-idle-rss-rca.md#L8-L31"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4048", "topic": "The corrected S23 `MemoryTracking` failure was generic ClickHouse boot w", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B020-022", "B020-023"], "canonical_claim": "The corrected S23 `MemoryTracking` failure was generic ClickHouse boot warmup: the non-leader `ch2` grew more than the leader despite running zero GC folds, and the CAS pool contained zero blobs, manifests, refs, and roots.; S23's tracked-memory growth decelerated after the first 90 seconds: `ch1` gained 56.6 MiB and then only 9.3 MiB during quiesce, while `ch2` gained 71.5 MiB and then only 4.7 MiB, which is a warmup curve rather than a constant-slope leak.", "issue_ids": ["S23"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s23-tracked-growth-rca.md#L18-L31", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s23-tracked-growth-rca.md#L9-L16"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4049", "topic": "S38 failed twice because no `ref_late_log_detected` event appeared durin", "target": "operations/monitoring", "member_ids": ["B021-011"], "canonical_claim": "S38 failed twice because no `ref_late_log_detected` event appeared during the 240-second post-injection poll window after injecting a dead-epoch late log at key `.../_log/0000000000000001-fffffffffffffffe`.", "issue_ids": ["S38"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s38-late-log-clamp-starvation.md#symptom"]}
